00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:45.600
A lot of you were asking me about the Yellowjacket
name because Hank Pym in the comics was Yellowjacket

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:47.250
for a while.

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:51.620
Yes, that’s true, the movie is changing
the backstory.

00:01:51.620 --> 00:01:58.780
In the comics Darren Cross had his own competing
company that went up against Stark Industries,

00:01:58.780 --> 00:02:00.550
Trask Industries and Oscorp.

00:02:00.550 --> 00:02:07.230
Eventually he started to die, performed crazy
surgery and as a result of a transplant, mutated

00:02:07.230 --> 00:02:17.460
and got minor powers.

00:02:17.460 --> 00:02:24.410
The character did cross over with the Scott
Lang Ant-Man when he was trying to find the

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:28.980
doctor that performed Cross’ life saving
surgery so she could do the same thing for

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:30.870
his daughter who was also dying.

00:02:30.870 --> 00:02:34.370
The movie is downplaying some of the Scott
Lang comic book backstory, but he still has

00:02:34.370 --> 00:02:35.370
a daughter.

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:43.920
If you’ve read the comic, just expect some
minor changes.

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:51.550
Hank Pym of course is played by Michael Douglas,
watching him old mansplain the movie at comic

00:02:51.550 --> 00:02:59.740
