00:04:04.370 --> 00:04:10.030
He enlists Scott Lang to help take down Darren
Cross and get his Pym Tech back.

00:04:10.030 --> 00:04:14.849
For those wondering about Edgar Wright’s
version of the movie, in his version Scott

00:04:14.849 --> 00:04:18.510
Lang was working at Hank Pym’s company as
a scientist.

00:04:18.510 --> 00:04:21.880
It didn’t involve the thief aspects of his
backstory as much.

00:04:21.880 --> 00:04:31.660
This version of the story plays a little more
on that, and Scott Lang isn’t quite as much

00:04:31.660 --> 00:04:33.250
of a Tony Stark type person.

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:41.970
He’s more average joe who gets swept up
in the heist adventure.

00:04:41.970 --> 00:04:44.750
We also see Hope Van Dyne, played by Evangeline
Lily.

00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:47.460
She’s also a big part of Team Pym in the
movie.

00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:51.820
Her mother is Janet Van Dyne, but in all of
the interviews everyone has done.

00:04:51.820 --> 00:04:53.800
They never mention Janet.

00:04:53.800 --> 00:04:56.460
So by all accounts, she’s probably not in
the movie in a big way.

00:04:56.460 --> 00:05:15.040
But she’ll probably be mentioned when Hank
and Hope have father daughter scenes.

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:18.900
I think we all just really want to know if
Hope is going to take the mantle from her

00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:29.010
mother and become The Wasp.

00:05:29.010 --> 00:05:32.820
There was a story arc in the comics where
an alternate universe version of Hope named

00:05:32.820 --> 00:05:36.070
Hope Pym became Red Queen, but she was kind
of a villain.

00:05:36.070 --> 00:05:38.840
So, just another small change to the comics.

00:05:38.840 --> 00:05:46.139
